  "description": "8-bit quasi-bidirectional I/O expander on the I2C bus, the chip behind nearly every I2C LCD 'backpack'. Three address pins (A0-A2) give eight selectable addresses, and an open-drain INT output flags input changes without polling. Operates 2.5-6 V. The ports are quasi-bidirectional (a weak internal pull-up to source, a strong pull-down to sink), so loads are normally wired active-low. The PCF8574A is identical but occupies a different address block.",
