  "typical_application": "Add 8 GPIO over I2C, or drive an HD44780 character LCD as an I2C 'backpack'; cascade up to 8 (PCF8574) plus 8 (PCF8574A) on one bus.",
  "gotchas": [
    "ports are QUASI-bidirectional: the internal pull-up sources only ~100 uA but the pull-down sinks ~25 mA, so wire LEDs/loads active-low (sink current), not active-high",
    "to use a pin as an input, first write a 1 to it (releasing it to the weak pull-up) - it has no separate direction register",
    "PCF8574 answers at 0x20-0x27 while the PCF8574A answers at 0x38-0x3F; mixing them up is the most common 'I2C device not found'",
    "no internal SDA/SCL pull-ups; the I2C bus needs external pull-up resistors",
    "INT is open-drain active-low and needs a pull-up; it asserts on any input change and clears on an I2C read"
  ],
